@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@ be reused. The ordinary ARM64 prelink interface remains available.
 The fileset emitter places the collection root at the native kernel's link
 address, marks the copied kernel as a fileset member, rebases metadata and
 keeps only the selected roots and their dependencies in the fileset index.
+Reviewed per-site bindings require native symbols only for sites within that
+selected dependency closure. A selected site with a missing symbol still stops
+emission; selecting every component retains the full fixture checks.
 The legacy `--slide` value does not apply to filesets. Rebuilt chains use
 virtual offsets, including across native BSS gaps.
 
@@ -79,3 +82,11 @@ The 24A446 fixture also pins `IOCircularDataQueueCopyLatest` and `get_aiotask`.
 A complete rebuild of the native adapter archives changed the RELEASE reference
 layout and lost these two order-based matches. Their original function digests,
 source consumers and accessor/copy semantics are recorded in the fixture.
+
+The 24A446 fixture records reviewed platform and CPU methods with full original function digests. Small accessors use byte-identical bodies after removing the original BTI entry, plus PAC identity and source fields. Forwarding methods record dispatch slots, argument flow and error returns. Shared override PAC values alone do not distinguish base methods from derived methods; the full body must establish the selected implementation. These records do not qualify hardware behavior.
+
+`emit_prelink.py --analysis-cache DIR` enables a trusted local decoded-image cache. Keys include full image content, Mach-O header and fixup scope, analysis implementation and Python version. Reviewed binding fixtures invalidate pairing maps independently while decoded inputs remain reusable. Corrupt cache entries are rebuilt; writes use atomic replacement. Keep this pickle directory local and trusted. Without the option, decoded inputs are still shared across reference-matching recursion in a single run. The existing exact-input map checks and strict missing-reference policy remain in effect.
+
+Reviewed 24A446 metadata bindings distinguish `Class::metaClass` constant pointer variables from their `Class::gMetaClass` objects. Getter and class-name initializer evidence identifies the pointee; native fixups verify the pointer level. Reviewed class-vtable bases additionally require class identity plus complete slot-count/authentication-layout agreement. A runtime virtual offset is relative to the address point (`vtable symbol + 16`), not the symbol base. This evidence identifies ABI layout and does not establish driver runtime compatibility.
+
+Checked-shape analysis also normalizes a single entry BTI C/J/JC landing hint when a body follows it. Interior BTI remains part of the shape, and an internal branch targeting the removed entry disables normalization. Emitted instructions are unchanged; unique matching and exact-input validation still apply.
